# Mutation cases for the vocabulary gate's exemption table — an entry names
# either a directory or one file, and it covers exactly that.
#
# Run with
# `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/scope_exemption_granularity.cases`.
#
# The gate's logic lives in its own test file, so that file is the target
# here. Both cases restore a shape the rule had until 2026-08-13.
#
# Why the rule changed: it used to demand a trailing `/` on every entry, and
# the reason given was that an entry "cannot match a sibling file by
# accident". Exact path equality serves that purpose strictly better, and
# demanding the slash inverted the intent — the only way to excuse one file
# was to excuse its whole directory, which is the accidental sibling
# coverage the rule existed to prevent. Exempting one driver under
# `backends/rust/tests/tests/` would have covered every driver beside it.
#
# A case that SURVIVES here means the new granularity is asserted by nothing.

mutation_tests -p sce-build --features cli --test scope_terminology
mutation_targets sce-build/tests/scope_terminology.rs

# ── A file entry reaches its siblings ──────────────────────────────
#
# The old matcher, restored: one comparison for both kinds of entry. Every
# current entry is a directory, so the sweep's verdict over this tree does
# not change at all — which is exactly why the algebra needs a unit test
# rather than the tree. `a/b/first.rs` would begin covering
# `a/b/first.rs.bak`, and a file entry would open a directory of the same
# stem.

mutation_case "a file exemption matches by prefix like a directory" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/tests/scope_terminology.rs",
     """    if prefix.ends_with('/') {
        rel.starts_with(prefix)
    } else {
        rel == prefix
    }""",
     "    rel.starts_with(prefix)")
PY

# ── A mistyped entry resolves to nothing, quietly ──────────────────
#
# Existence dropped. A typo then exempts nothing while looking registered,
# and the sweep's own staleness check reports it as "an exemption covering
# nothing" — a message about a dead entry for what is really a misspelling.
# Nothing in the table can supply the typo, so deleting this check changes
# no verdict unless something asks it about a path that is wrong on purpose.

mutation_case "an exemption is not checked for existing" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/tests/scope_terminology.rs",
     "fn exemption_resolves(root: &Path, prefix: &str) -> Result<(), String> {",
     """fn exemption_resolves(root: &Path, prefix: &str) -> Result<(), String> {
    if true {
        let _ = (root, prefix);
        return Ok(());
    }""")
PY
